# Topical events

Gather a time-bounded household subject on one page, with its purpose, dates and status stated. A reader must be able to tell current work from finished work. For example, a fictional “Replace the hall thermostat” project shows its dates and status, and leaves live alerts to Home Assistant. The government crisis and policy context of the source does not transfer to a household.

## When to use it

Use it for a planned maintenance project, a seasonal setup or a documented upgrade. State the purpose, dates and current status, and keep background apart from live alerts and operational controls.

## Structure and behaviour

Use a concise introduction, current information and a curated list of related guides or records. An [About page](topical-events/about.html) may explain scope and responsibility. Mark closed projects and keep their history where it helps. A decorative image is optional and needs a clear purpose.

## Home Assistant boundary

Do not invent a campaign, crisis response or multi-agency authority. This is reference guidance, not an event-management feature or automation scheduler. The examples are fictional and no household dates are inferred.

